OK. I just use standard distributed nethack. "typedef short int schar;"
sits there, right in the middle of config.h. By default commented out.
But nethack has been probably ported to more different machines/system
than any other piece of software known to me - and some of them will
require that you uncomment this small line. And it will still be standard
nethack. With possibility of getting AC=-1000 (by wearing +1009 gauntlets
of power, for instance - plusses on armor are also schar...). Of course
normal player will never be able to get such low AC without cheating, and
I seriously doubt it could be useful (and I seriously doubt that the game
will be interesting)... But it will be standard official nethack...

